Subtract a deleted document's length, not its length code, in VACUUM

Applies to vchord_bm25 0.3.0 (upstream tag 0.3.0, commit c610b7ab).

The metapage keeps doc_term_cnt, the sum of document lengths, and BM25 takes
the average document length from it. An insert adds the document's exact
length (insert.rs) and a build sums exact lengths (builder.rs), but
ambulkdelete (vacuum.rs) subtracts field_norm_reader.read(i): the document's
one-byte length code, not its length. The code equals the length only up to
40; above that it compresses (136 to 143 is code 62, 300 is code 72). So every
deleted document longer than 40 leaves most of its length behind, and the
average document length grows with every update and delete that VACUUM cleans
up, until the index is rebuilt.

The index stores only the code, so the fix subtracts the length the code
stands for, id_to_fieldnorm(code). The code maps a length down to the start of
its bucket, so a deleted document now leaves behind less than its bucket's
width (under 7 at a length of 139, instead of about 77), and nothing at a
length that starts a bucket, such as 64. A rebuild still resets the sum
exactly. No on-disk format or SQL changes.

Measured: 1,000 rows inserted, deleted and vacuumed left doc_term_cnt at
915,973 against 2,973 true, an average length of 3,578 against 11.61.

License: this patch modifies vchord_bm25 and is offered under the same terms
as vchord_bm25 itself: AGPL-3.0-only or Elastic-2.0, at the recipient's option.
---
diff --git a/src/index/vacuum.rs b/src/index/vacuum.rs
index fc449a4..c107de0 100644
--- a/src/index/vacuum.rs
+++ b/src/index/vacuum.rs
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ use crate::{
     page::{page_read, page_write, BM25_PAGE_SIZE, METAPAGE_BLKNO},
     segment::{
         delete::DeleteBitmapReader,
-        field_norm::{FieldNormRead, FieldNormReader},
+        field_norm::{id_to_fieldnorm, FieldNormRead, FieldNormReader},
         growing::GrowingSegmentReader,
         meta::MetaPageData,
         payload::PayloadReader,
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ pub unsafe extern "C-unwind" fn ambulkdelete(
         if callback(tid) {
             delete_bitmap_reader.delete(i);
             meta.doc_cnt -= 1;
-            meta.doc_term_cnt -= field_norm_reader.read(i) as u64;
+            meta.doc_term_cnt -= id_to_fieldnorm(field_norm_reader.read(i)) as u64;
             stats.tuples_removed += 1.0;
         } else {
             stats.num_index_tuples += 1.0;
